                "username": "fornchu110"
            },
            "kind": "NO_CODE_CHANGE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "Makes sense to me."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/entity_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 704,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "You can also simplify the reading from the message as well.\n\n```suggestion\n            auto [path, interfaces] = msg.unpack<sdbusplus::message::object_path, std::vector<std::string>>();\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/entity_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 704,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "Thank you for the suggestion; I\u2019ve updated the changes accordingly."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/entity_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 711,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Can we remove the match on the path directly or should we check which interface was removed?\n\nIt should work for `xyz.openbmc_project.FruDevice`, but will it still work if there are multiple interfaces.\n\nFor example, probe interfaces are `{I1}` and there are other unrelated interfaces `{I2}`.\n\n`/example/e1` has interfaces `I1` and `I2`\n\n-> properties changed match is created on `/example/e1`\n\n`/example/e1` has interface `I2` removed\n\n-> `/example/e1` has their properties changed match removed.\n\n-> `propertiesChangedCallback` is not triggered since `I2` is not a probe interface\n\n-> `/example/e1` has a property change on `I1`\n\n-> the property change should cause a configuration change, but does not, due to the missing D-Bus match.\n\n\nI was just wondering about this case, maybe someone can tell if it's a real problem or i got the wrong idea."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/entity_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 711,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "Thank you for the suggestion.\nIn the latest patchset, I\u2019ve changed the logic to erase the D\u2011Bus match only when a probe interface is removed, rather than on any interface change.\nThis should resolve the leak and cover the corner case\u2014does this align with your expectations?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/entity_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 711,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes, thank you \ud83d\ude0a"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/entity_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 712,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "flat_map has an erase() that takes the key that would simplify this to 1 line."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/entity_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 712,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Yang",
                        "email": "eric.yang.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "fornchu110"
                    },
                    "message": "Thank you for the suggestion; I\u2019ve updated the changes accordingly."
                }
            ],
